# SENERE --------------------------------------------------------

- Make sure only one term set can use the hovedkort at any one time
- Add possibility to have 6. ferieuge / Feriefridage 

*** Analytics Page: ***
- On the rate history you should be able to click the records, which would expand showing the extra things that are counted in the total rate (such as company pension contrib, fritvalgskonto etc.+)
- Is there anything you think could be helpful to add?
- It seems like the workplace table showing Salaried H does not work with the proration.
- Rework of Actual, Planned, Projection
- - All salaried hours are planned, not projected. Projections are only for hourly positions
- - In my currently loaded data, for july and august, it seems there is a mix of projection and planned hours, but it seems like my approved JKF shifts for july is not shown in the graph.
- Hovering over the months should show the total gross/net amounts

- Remove the limit on one active contract per workplace. -- for some workplaces it makes sense that you might have two active jobs that are more or less unrelated and has wildly different terms.
- - Each _active_ contract should have their own chip in the planning mode (contracts may have different hour goals etc.)
- - Define somewhere if different contracts at one workplace share the same payslip (summed hours)
- - Maybe add some way to easily know the contracts apart in the workplace avatar.
- - maybe the user could specify per contract: a color and/or an icon or a short (max 2 char) identifier -- the user would be prompted when there are overlapping contracts. Can be changed in the customize menu.

- A page I can use to transfer shift info to whatever kind of system the workplace uses for me to report my hours
- - Should be customizable. Example at JKF i report hours in an excel sheet with cols Date, week, month, hours, break(30 min, yes/no), name. This transfer would be easiest with an excel-compatible copy-paste.
- at JKF if there are multiple shifts in one day, I add them toghether to one per date. This should also be user configurable. Maybe implement some kind of simple templating/scripting thing?

- Workplace detail page — multi-rate months. The detail still renders a single term set's payslip (the mid-month rate). For a mid-month raise it shows one rate's slice (~30000), not the full 70000 the main dashboard shows. Making it sum multiple rates means reworking the payslip breakdown UI (feriepenge/pension/tax lines are built for one rate). Biggest remaining item.

- Formal payslip (PayslipService). Still uses the full monthly salary — not prorated for partial months or multiple rates. Separate from the dashboards you flagged.

- Net-tax approximation. Earned/planned and multi-term-set nets each apply the full monthly tax deduction per slice (same approximation the hourly path already used). Gross is exact; combined net can be slightly overstated. Correct-but-harder fix: tax the summed monthly gross once.

- (from the 2026-07-08 audit) Back-to-back contracts within one month: active_termset_in_month picks only the latest-starting contract, so if contract A ends on the 10th and contract B starts on the 20th, the month's salaried figures omit A's partial-month pay. Related to the multi-rate item above.

- (from the 2026-07-08 audit) Decide the fate of the orphaned calendar pages: calendar_view "month" and "payroll period" views + 3 templates (month.html, payroll_period.html, payroll_period_select.html) are URL-reachable but linked from nowhere. Keep (add nav links) or delete.

*** Main Dashboard: ***
- On the hour goal-statcard, when hovering over the grey portion of the progress bar, it should show the hour deficit(if any), ie how far you are from the goal, not just the goal.
- The message "2 shifts in February belong to March payroll (19,70h)" is nice, but maybe you can click to expand, so it shows the shifts/dates and the hours? -- maybe hovering over it and/or clicking highlights the shifts if they are visible on the calendar.

*** All Calendars: ***
- Possibility to change to a list view where each shift is a row in a list/table

*** Changes to Workplace dashboard: ***
- Add a button that includes planned shifts in the stats etc.
- The month picker should be at the top, just under the workplace name.
- Back-button: if you change the month, the back button should not go back to the month you were on bekeep fore, it should go back to the main dashboard or workplaces overview.
- The calendar and the shift-cards within should be changed to behave more like the shift chips in the planning calendar

*** Changes to Payslip Editor ***
- Buttons to change month
- Add the net hourly wage (net pay / total hours)
- Net pay is always in the bottom and gross pay is always in the top
- Custom lines default placement: New deduction lines are placed after subtotal(after tax), addition lines are placed just under gross pay
- Automatic recalculation after each change (when creating/removing or moving a custom line.) -- remove the manual recalculate button.

- Implementation question: I don't understand the payroll / generate period page. The payslip editor was created in order to adjust for additions/deductions on the payslip that would change the net amount. This would also help with singular month bonusses or variable bonusses, but I do not understand the payroll page.

*** Changes to workplace calendar: ***
- Work shifts for days that are before the start or after the end of the payroll period should be greyed out on the calendar. -- just like on the planning calendar
- When clicking the calendar, currently it opens a modal, i would like this to appear as a pop-up just over the date you clicked (like the pick-workplace-popup on the planning calendar)
- If no work shifts are already on the current day, it should automatically open the dialogue to add a new shift
- There should be a date field, so you can change it if you click the wrong date
- At the top of the add work shift form, there should be a small banner showing which workplace you are adding a shift for.
- In the add work shift form, it should show the shift time in minutes and decimal with and without the break
- When you are done adding a work shift, you should be returned to the workplace dashboard, not the main dashboard.

- In the workplace settings, there should be a break policy configuration, where you can pick:
-- Break time is paid
-- Break time is static (ie you can only enter yes/no in the work shift configuration, and the break numbers are static)
-- Break time is variable and should be entered manually every time (like it is now)

